The following rules complete the state model:
- IDLE, NAVIGATING, AVOIDING_OBSTACLE, DELIVERING, and RETURNING may enter SAFE_MODE if a critical trigger occurs.
- NAVIGATING, AVOIDING_OBSTACLE, DELIVERING, and RETURNING may enter LINK_LOST if communication supervision fails.
- LINK_LOST must still monitor local sensors and battery conditions. A local critical event must not be ignored merely because Mission Control is unreachable.
- SAFE_MODE must inhibit delivery release and ordinary mission commands.
- Recovery from SAFE_MODE requires fault clearance and verification. Recovery from LINK_LOST requires link restoration, session validation, and safe command reconciliation.
A robust implementation should model the robot's motion state and its communication/safety status as orthogonal state machines. This avoids ambiguous behaviour when communication loss and a safety fault occur simultaneously.
